  "goodToKnow": "Der Putsch is a coup d'état: ein Militärputsch, einen Putsch vereiteln (to thwart a coup). The word came from Swiss German, meaning a blow or push, and English borrowed it. Famous German examples: the Kapp-Putsch of 1920 in Berlin and the Hitlerputsch of November 1923 in Munich. In December 2022, police raided Reichsbürger groups accused of planning a coup. Plural: die Putsche."
